Reference patch — ORT core AppContainer external-data fixes
===========================================================

Target: microsoft/onnxruntime @ tag v1.24.4 (matches Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime.DirectML
        1.24.4 pinned in uwp/packages.config).

Two independent fixes for loading ONNX models with external `.onnx.data` on the
Xbox UWP AppContainer (`docs/uwp-constraints.md §8`, `docs/fp16-extdata-runbook.md`):

1. `onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc` (`ValidateExternalDataPath`):
   guard `weakly_canonical()`. On the AppContainer, MSVC STL walks the path from
   the drive root and hits the inaccessible `Q:\Users\UserMgr0` segment →
   `ACCESS_DENIED` → crash. Use the std::error_code overload + `lexically_normal`
   fallback (the file is a trusted, already-present local file).

2. `onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.cc` (`ReadFileIntoBuffer`): reduce the
   read chunk `k_max_bytes_to_read` from 1 GB to 16 MB. A single ~0.5-1 GB
   `ReadFile` (e.g. the un-quantized `embed_tokens.weight`, vocab 128k × hidden ×
   fp16/fp32) makes the kernel lock that many pages into physical memory (MDL) for
   the transfer; under AppContainer memory pressure this exceeds resources →
   `errcode 1450` (ERROR_NO_SYSTEM_RESOURCES), intermittently. mmap can't help:
   ORT's `MapFileIntoMemory` uses the non-`-FromApp` Win32 APIs, which the
   AppContainer blocks, so ORT always falls back to this ReadFile path. 16 MB
   chunks lock few pages and always stay within resources; this is what actually
   lets fp16 `.onnx.data` >2 GB load.

Applied by scripts/vendor-ort-extdata-patch.ps1 (prefers `git apply`, else a
context-tolerant in-place transform, then verifies both changes before building).
If `git apply` rejects this reference diff (upstream context drift), regenerate it
against the pinned checkout — the semantic changes are the edits below.

--- a/onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc
@@ namespace onnxruntime {
+// xllama (AppContainer): std::filesystem::weakly_canonical() walks path segments
+// from the drive root and throws ACCESS_DENIED on the inaccessible
+// Q:\Users\UserMgr0 segment (docs/uwp-constraints.md §8), crashing model load.
+// Use the std::error_code overload and fall back to a purely lexical
+// normalization when the walk is denied — the external-data file is a trusted
+// local file that already exists.
+static std::filesystem::path XllamaSafeCanonical(const std::filesystem::path& p) {
+  std::error_code ec;
+  std::filesystem::path r = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(p, ec);
+  if (ec || r.empty()) {
+    return p.lexically_normal();
+  }
+  return r;
+}
+
 Status ValidateExternalDataPath(const std::filesystem::path& base_dir,
                                 const std::filesystem::path& location,
                                 const std::filesystem::path& model_path) {
@@ ValidateExternalDataPath
-    auto base_canonical = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(base_dir);
+    auto base_canonical = XllamaSafeCanonical(base_dir);
@@
-    auto resolved = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(base_dir / location);
+    auto resolved = XllamaSafeCanonical(base_dir / location);
@@
-        auto real_model_dir = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(model_path).parent_path();
+        auto real_model_dir = XllamaSafeCanonical(model_path).parent_path();

--- a/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/platform/windows/env.cc
@@ WindowsEnv::ReadFileIntoBuffer
   size_t total_bytes_read = 0;
   while (total_bytes_read < length) {
-    constexpr DWORD k_max_bytes_to_read = 1 << 30;  // read at most 1GB each time
+    constexpr DWORD k_max_bytes_to_read = 1 << 24;  // xllama: 16 MB — a 1 GB ReadFile locks too many pages in the Xbox AppContainer (errcode 1450)
     const size_t bytes_remaining = length - total_bytes_read;
     const DWORD bytes_to_read = static_cast<DWORD>(std::min<size_t>(bytes_remaining, k_max_bytes_to_read));
